			<div class="content" id="post-content-4405996">
									

<p>This was a weird one for me.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>On the one hand, this was pretty damn funny, and multiple different lines got an audible chuckle out of me, so this was a success on that front.</p>
<p>On the other hand, I have a few issues and nitpicks with the piece that hindered my enjoyment.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>posted by dado</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This whole image is funny, but this bit here feels like a total cop out for why you don't have a picture of an actual Roomba anywhere in the article, which just wasn't necessary. It's answering a question that wasn't asked quite obviously.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This event has lead to the theory that SCP-4451-1 functions as an extremely large atom undergoing rapid and continuous radioactive decay and that the gel facilitates the transfer of energy to the vacuum cleaner2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;Okay so I get that dado is an anomalous pharmacologist, but you go way too deep into the irl science here without actually demonstrating that you understand the words you're using. Atoms aren't that big and no self respecting scientist would propose or accept a solution like this without veritable proof, of which there is none. Things can be radioactive without being a single atom undergoing decay. In fact, the more atoms decaying, the better. This is some bad nuclear physics here and it distracted me quite a bit. The image and the vapo rub cracked me up though, I gotta say.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a pharmaceutical billionaire and anti-government advocate.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't see the relevance of the anti-government bit? Are you trying to say he's an anarchocapitalist? Either way, why?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>dado is not as good of engineer as medicine maker, in fact, tsar roomba is dado's first try but dado very proud of tsar roomba (by dado)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't feel like dado speak. It feels like an ESL person speaking in the third person. dado tends to vary his grammatical errors erroneously and the note reads at bit to formulaic with the errors to capture that spontaneous nature of dado. It's better than others I've seen but there's room for improvement here.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I'm left feeling a novote on this one. It does the humor super well but it flubs some other aspects of the execution that leaves me a bit disappointed.</p>
<p>ETA: Seeing as my primary issue of the bad science was taken care of, I'll gladly upvote this now. Good job, author!</p>
<p><span style="font-size:smaller;"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> <em>Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1571978230" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;">TheMightyMcB</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1571978230" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</em></span></p>

