					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2104082); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2104082&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200841" alt="ManyMeats" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2104082)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2104082); return false;" >ManyMeats</a></span> <span class="odate time_1572012488 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Oct 2019 14:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4406609">
									

<p>I've thought about what to say on this for a while now and I am still not 100% sure how to feel. On the one hand, many parts of this are entertaining and did get me to smile or snort a little. But on the other hand, the repeated skirting if IRL science <em>and getting it wrong</em> really rubs me the wrong way in a manner that seriously kneecaps this piece.</p>
<p>The general use of dado is just &quot;okay&quot; at best for me. You clearly know the <em>what</em> of dado but the finer points of adopting and using the character seem to be beyond the reach of this piece. To me, this comes off as someone clearly trying to write dado, rather than being a dado SCP if that makes any sense. I can go into this in more detail but it would require an analysis and comparison well beyond the scope of a Site Crit review.</p>
<p>Overall, I had to -1. This piece could do with probably 30-40% of the material being trimmed out and not suffer for it.</p>

